## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Onboarding
## Notes: Sane UI's setup, step by step: a window that walks you through what a module shows and lets you choose how you want it, with a sample that changes as you choose. Sane UI reads it only when a setup opens: by itself the first time a module is on, from a module's options page, or /sane setup. Comes with Sane UI.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## Group: SaneUI
## Dependencies: SaneUI
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\SaneUI_Onboarding\Art\icon
## X-License: MIT

# The module's own table and its words; a module's setup shown (Show)
Onboarding.lua
# The controls of a step: the module's own switches, numbers and choices, set through Core as its options page sets them
Controls.lua
# The window: the module's sample at its left, the step's head, words and controls at its right, Back and Next under them
Window.lua
